@anon.e792752b4454889dead1a66caae2c60f.411 = private unnamed_addr constant [752 x i8] c"A list of mappings from glob-style file pattern to Python version to use when checking the\0Acorresponding file(s).\0A\0AThis may be useful for overriding the global Python version settings in `target-version` or\0A`requires-python` for a subset of files. For example, if you have a project with a minimum\0Asupported Python version of 3.9 but a subdirectory of developer scripts that want to use a\0Anewer feature like the `match` statement from Python 3.10, you can use\0A`per-file-target-version` to specify `\22developer_scripts/*.py\22 = \22py310\22`.\0A\0AThis setting is used by the linter to enforce any enabled version-specific lint rules, as\0Awell as by the formatter for any version-specific formatting options, such as parenthesizing\0Acontext managers on Python 3.10+.", align 1
