@anon.e792752b4454889dead1a66caae2c60f.427 = private unnamed_addr constant [772 x i8] c"The line length to use when enforcing long-lines violations (like `E501`)\0Aand at which `isort` and the formatter prefers to wrap lines.\0A\0AThe length is determined by the number of characters per line, except for lines containing East Asian characters or emojis.\0AFor these lines, the [unicode width](https://unicode.org/reports/tr11/) of each character is added up to determine the length.\0A\0AThe value must be greater than `0` and less than or equal to `320`.\0A\0ANote: While the formatter will attempt to format lines such that they remain\0Awithin the `line-length`, it isn't a hard upper bound, and formatted lines may\0Aexceed the `line-length`.\0A\0ASee [`pycodestyle.max-line-length`](#lint_pycodestyle_max-line-length) to configure different lengths for `E501` and the formatter.", align 1
