@anon.e792752b4454889dead1a66caae2c60f.521 = private unnamed_addr constant [635 x i8] c"A list of objects that should be treated equivalently to a `logging.Logger` object.\0A\0AThis is useful for ensuring proper diagnostics (e.g., to identify `logging` deprecations and other best-practices) for projects that re-export a `logging.Logger` object from a common module.\0A\0AFor example, if you have a module `logging_setup.py` with the following contents: ```python import logging\0A\0Alogger = logging.getLogger(__name__) ```\0A\0AAdding `\22logging_setup.logger\22` to `logger-objects` will ensure that `logging_setup.logger` is treated as a `logging.Logger` object when imported from other modules (e.g., `from logging_setup import logger`).", align 1
