@anon.e792752b4454889dead1a66caae2c60f.1335 = private unnamed_addr constant [368 x i8] c"A list of names (or patterns) to ignore when considering `pep8-naming` violations.\0A\0ASupports glob patterns. For example, to ignore all names starting with `test_` or ending with `_test`, you could use `ignore-names = [\22test_*\22, \22*_test\22]`. For more information on the glob syntax, refer to the [`globset` documentation](https://docs.rs/globset/latest/globset/#syntax).", align 1
@anon.e792752b4454889dead1a66caae2c60f.1336 = private unnamed_addr constant [452 x i8] c"Additional names (or patterns) to ignore when considering `pep8-naming` violations, in addition to those included in [`ignore-names`](#lint_pep8-naming_ignore-names).\0A\0ASupports glob patterns. For example, to ignore all names starting with `test_` or ending with `_test`, you could use `ignore-names = [\22test_*\22, \22*_test\22]`. For more information on the glob syntax, refer to the [`globset` documentation](https://docs.rs/globset/latest/globset/#syntax).", align 1
@anon.e792752b4454889dead1a66caae2c60f.1337 = private unnamed_addr constant [528 x i8] c"A list of decorators that, when applied to a method, indicate that the method should be treated as a class method (in addition to the builtin `@classmethod`).\0A\0AFor example, Ruff will expect that any method decorated by a decorator in this list takes a `cls` argument as its first argument.\0A\0AExpects to receive a list of fully-qualified names (e.g., `pydantic.validator`, rather than `validator`) or alternatively a plain name which is then matched against the last segment in case the decorator itself consists of a dotted name.", align 1
