@anon.e792752b4454889dead1a66caae2c60f.1340 = private unnamed_addr constant [914 x i8] c"The maximum line length to allow for [`line-too-long`](https://docs.astral.sh/ruff/rules/line-too-long/) violations. By default,\0Athis is set to the value of the [`line-length`](#line-length) option.\0A\0AUse this option when you want to detect extra-long lines that the formatter can't automatically split by setting\0A`pycodestyle.line-length` to a value larger than [`line-length`](#line-length).\0A\0A```toml\0A# The formatter wraps lines at a length of 88.\0Aline-length = 88\0A\0A[pycodestyle]\0A# E501 reports lines that exceed the length of 100.\0Amax-line-length = 100\0A```\0A\0AThe length is determined by the number of characters per line, except for lines containing East Asian characters or emojis.\0AFor these lines, the [unicode width](https://unicode.org/reports/tr11/) of each character is added up to determine the length.\0A\0ASee the [`line-too-long`](https://docs.astral.sh/ruff/rules/line-too-long/) rule for more information.", align 1
