@anon.e792752b4454889dead1a66caae2c60f.1520 = private unnamed_addr constant [817 x i8] c"A list of file patterns to exclude from formatting in addition to the files excluded globally (see [`exclude`](#exclude), and [`extend-exclude`](#extend-exclude)).\0A\0AExclusions are based on globs, and can be either:\0A\0A- Single-path patterns, like `.mypy_cache` (to exclude any directory\0A  named `.mypy_cache` in the tree), `foo.py` (to exclude any file named\0A  `foo.py`), or `foo_*.py` (to exclude any file matching `foo_*.py` ).\0A- Relative patterns, like `directory/foo.py` (to exclude that specific\0A  file) or `directory/*.py` (to exclude any Python files in\0A  `directory`). Note that these paths are relative to the project root\0A  (e.g., the directory containing your `pyproject.toml`).\0A\0AFor more information on the glob syntax, refer to the [`globset` documentation](https://docs.rs/globset/latest/globset/#syntax).", align 1
