@anon.e792752b4454889dead1a66caae2c60f.1535 = private unnamed_addr constant [1134 x i8] c"Configures the preferred quote character for strings. The recommended options are\0A\0A* `double` (default): Use double quotes `\22`\0A* `single`: Use single quotes `'`\0A\0AIn compliance with [PEP 8](https://peps.python.org/pep-0008/) and [PEP 257](https://peps.python.org/pep-0257/),\0ARuff prefers double quotes for triple quoted strings and docstrings even when using `quote-style = \22single\22`.\0A\0ARuff deviates from using the configured quotes if doing so prevents the need for\0Aescaping quote characters inside the string:\0A\0A```python\0Aa = \22a string without any quotes\22\0Ab = \22It's monday morning\22\0A```\0A\0ARuff will change the quotes of the string assigned to `a` to single quotes when using `quote-style = \22single\22`.\0AHowever, Ruff uses double quotes for the string assigned to `b` because using single quotes would require escaping the `'`,\0Awhich leads to the less readable code: `'It\\'s monday morning'`.\0A\0AIn addition, Ruff supports the quote style `preserve` for projects that already use\0Aa mixture of single and double quotes and can't migrate to the `double` or `single` style.\0AThe quote style `preserve` leaves the quotes of all strings unchanged.", align 1
