@anon.e792752b4454889dead1a66caae2c60f.1542 = private unnamed_addr constant [657 x i8] c"Ruff uses existing trailing commas as an indication that short lines should be left separate.\0AIf this option is set to `true`, the magic trailing comma is ignored.\0A\0AFor example, Ruff leaves the arguments separate even though\0Acollapsing the arguments to a single line doesn't exceed the line length if `skip-magic-trailing-comma = false`:\0A\0A```python\0A# The arguments remain on separate lines because of the trailing comma after `b`\0Adef test(\0A    a,\0A    b,\0A): pass\0A```\0A\0ASetting `skip-magic-trailing-comma = true` changes the formatting to:\0A\0A```python\0A# The arguments remain on separate lines because of the trailing comma after `b`\0Adef test(a, b):\0A    pass\0A```", align 1
